  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hydroboration&ndash;oxidation is an anti-Markovnikov reaction, with the hydroxyl group attaching to the less-substituted carbon.&nbsp;In an oxymercuration&ndash;demercuration reaction, an alkene is treated with mercury(II) acetate, and the product is treated with sodium borohydride. The net result is a Markovnikov addition product in which the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OH</mi></math> group bonds to the more substituted carbon atom of the alkene.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b63e8a8f-a144-4e79-be87-a2df77fa8574-9894280_5.PNG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 180px;\" /></p>",
